////////////////////////////////Mesh_Input.txt////////////////////////////////////////////
Mesh indexing:
	i: 0->N-1 from left to right
	j: 0->M-1 from bottom to top
	n = i*M + j


////////////////////////////////Boundary_Input.txt////////////////////////////////////////////
The boundaries of the domain must be named:
	> Front
	> Back
	> Top 
	> Bottom
The boundaries of the obstacle must be named:
	> Obj_Front
	> Obj_Back
	> Obj_Top
	> Obj_Bottom
	(!) The obstacle boundaries must be removed when using the case without obstacle
	
Current limitation(!!!!!!): The Boundary Input format is designed so that any custom boundaries can be set. However, the operators functionality only works with the pre-set names listed above
		
////////////////////////////////Physical_BoCos.txt////////////////////////////////////////////
Assigns a type of boundary condition (Dirichlet or Neumann) to the boundaries defined in Boundary_Input.txt

////////////////////////////////SOlver_Input.txt////////////////////////////////////////////
Selects a solver to use

